person "==Player\n<size:16>[Person]</size>\n\nPlays the game on a phone or desktop browser." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxQZXJzb24=>> as Player
rectangle "==Room Service\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>\n\nLets friends play one world together (server/): a Cloudflare Worker that makes rooms and a Durable Object per shared world that keeps the world and each player's progress, checks every message, and relays positions and edits between up to 100 players. The moderator can make a copy of a world to play as one of its players (server/src/copy.js), apart from the real one, download a whole world as a backup file and put a world that's gone back from one (server/src/backup.js), and has a page listing every world's players, sortable by progress (server/src/admin.js). See server/README.md for the rules and security limits." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxTb2Z0d2FyZSBTeXN0ZW0=>> as RoomService
rectangle "==Development Tooling\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>\n\nTest harnesses and the deploy pipeline. Zero dependencies." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxTb2Z0d2FyZSBTeXN0ZW0sVG9vbGluZw==>> as DevelopmentTooling

rectangle "MORE THAN ENOUGH\n<size:16>[Software System]</size>" <<Boundary-TU9SRSBUSEFOIEVOT1VHSA==>> {
  rectangle "==Default Texture Pack\n<size:16>[Container: JSON + SVG]</size>\n\nLanternlight (packs/default/): pack.json mapping every thing in the Catalog to its SVG pictures and colours. Required before the game draws anything; players' packs override any part of it." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.DefaultTexturePack
  rectangle "==Wiki\n<size:16>[Container: HTML/CSS/JavaScript modules]</size>\n\nThe player documentation (wiki/), served next to the game. The game teaches nothing in-game, so every mechanic is written up here; tables and figures are rendered at load time from the Simulation Core's content and tuning, so they can never drift from the game. An Ideas page (ideas.js) collects possible directions for the game, clearly marked as not in it. Everything in the game is listed from the Catalog with its default pictures, and the texture pack format is documented." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.Wiki
  rectangle "==Translations\n<size:16>[Container: JavaScript modules (browser + Node)]</size>\n\nEvery word the player reads, in English and Lithuanian (src/i18n/, plus the wiki's own in wiki/i18n/). Historical release notes load on demand through news-text.js; startup retains current release prose. Code asks for text by key with t(); the language is picked once at load (the player's choice, else the browser's) and switching reloads the page. A missing key or placeholder throws, and the unit tests fail if either language lacks a key or any text bypasses t()." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.Translations
  rectangle "==Simulation Core\n<size:16>[Container: JavaScript modules (browser + Node)]</size>\n\nThe game rules (src/core/). Pure and deterministic: no DOM, no clock, no Math.random. Terrain is a pure function of (x, y, z, seed), state is a plain object, and the same modules run in the browser and in Node tests." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsQ29yZSBFbmdpbmU=>> as MORETHANENOUGH.SimulationCore
  rectangle "==Web Application\n<size:16>[Container: HTML/CSS/JavaScript modules]</size>\n\nThe presentation layer (index.html, style.css, src/game/). Owns the DOM, the canvas, input, audio, HUD and sheets, and localStorage. Reads state from the Simulation Core every frame and changes it only through the Core's exports." <<Element-RWxlbWVudCxDb250YWluZXIsUHJlc2VudGF0aW9u>> as MORETHANENOUGH.WebApplication
}

